---js
// <script>
let headerTitle = "Eleventy is a simpler <code>static</code> site generator";
let layout = "layouts/main.njk";

let searchTitle = "Eleventy is a simpler static site generator";

let eleventyImport = {
	collections: ["blog"]
};

let eleventyComputed = {
	social: {
		description: () => "Eleventy is a simpler static site generator."
	},
};
// </script>
---
<script webc:setup>
export function getHighlightedBlogPostContent(collection) {
	let posts = findBy(collection, 'data.blogHighlight', true);
	if(!posts.length) {
		return "";
	}
	posts.reverse();

	let content = [];
	let index = 0;
	for(let post of posts) {
		content.push(`<li><a href="${post.url}">${index === 0 ? `<strong>` : ""}${post.data.newstitle}${index === 0 ? `</strong>` : ""}</a> (<em>${newsDate(post.date)}</em>)</li>`);
		index++;
	}
	// 10 hardcoded posts on the blog
	content.push(`<li>…and <a href="/blog/">${collection.length + 10 - posts.length} more on the <strong>blog archives</strong></a>.</li>`)

	return `${content.join("")}`;
}
</script>

<!--- this is a workaround for the layout used in the header --->
<flex-luthor webc:nokeep></flex-luthor>

<div class="home-stats">
	<div class="home-stats-item">
		<div class="elv-callout">
			<div class="elv-callout-c">
				<download-counter :@value="npmProjectDownloads.downloads" :per-year="npmProjectDownloads.downloadsLastYear" :generated-at="npmProjectDownloads.generatedAt">Downloads all time<br>All npm packages</download-counter>
			</div>
		</div>
		<!-- <p class="home-stats-sub"><span @text="commaNumber(npmProjectDownloads.downloadsLastYear)"></span><span>Downloads last year</span></p> -->
	</div>
	<!-- <div class="home-stats-item">
		<div class="elv-callout">
			<div class="elv-callout-c">
				<download-counter :@value="npmProjectDownloads.stars" :per-year="npmProjectDownloads.starsPerYear" :generated-at="npmProjectDownloads.generatedAt" icon="star">GitHub<br>stars</download-counter>
			</div>
		</div>
		<p class="home-stats-sub"><span @text="commaNumber(npmProjectDownloads.closedIssues + npmProjectDownloads.closedPRs)"></span><span><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i><span class="sr-only">Closed </span>issues and PRs</span></p>
	</div> -->
	<!-- <div class="home-stats-item">
		<div class="elv-callout">
			<a href="https://osv.dev/list?ecosystem=npm&q=%4011ty%2Feleventy" class="elv-callout-c home-stats-link elv-externalexempt">
				<i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved download-counter-icon"></i>
				<span class="download-counter-num">0</span>
				<span class="download-counter-label">Security advisories<br>on core since 2017</span>
			</a>
		</div>
	</div> -->
</div>
<style>
.home-stats {
	display: flex;
	flex-wrap: wrap;
	align-items: flex-start;
	gap: .5em 1em;
	margin-block: 0 1em;
	margin-inline: -1rem;
}
.home-stats > * {
	flex-grow: 1;
	margin: 0;
}
/* Subgrid columns (icon, count, label) line up the all-time row with the counter inside the callout. */
.home-stats-link {
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	gap: .75em;
	color: inherit;
	text-decoration: none;
}
/* Keeps the taller rings from stretching the callout past the others. */
speedlify2-median {
	margin-block: -.5em;
}
/* Reserves the size of the five rings until the element is defined. */
speedlify2-median:not(:defined) {
	display: inline-block;
	width: 13.535em;
	height: 2.467em;
}
.home-stats-item {
	display: grid;
	grid-template-columns: auto auto 1fr;
	column-gap: .75em;
}
.home-stats-item > *,
.home-stats-item .elv-callout-c,
.home-stats-item download-counter {
	display: grid;
	grid-template-columns: subgrid;
	grid-column: 1 / -1;
}
.home-stats-item > .elv-callout {
	margin: 0;
	/* The callout paints --callout-secondary, which defaults to the page background */
	--callout-secondary: #f7f7f7;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
	.home-stats-item > .elv-callout {
		--callout-secondary: #262626;
	}
}
.home-stats-sub {
	align-items: baseline;
	margin: .25em 0 0;
	font-size: .6666666667em;
	opacity: .7;
}
.home-stats-sub > span:first-of-type {
	grid-column: 2;
	font-family: Roboto Mono, monospace;
	font-size: 1.375em;
	text-align: end;
}
.home-stats-sub .fa11ty-icon {
	margin-inline-start: 0;
}
.home-stats-sub > :last-child {
	text-transform: uppercase;
	letter-spacing: .1em;
}
</style>

<quick-start></quick-start>

<div webc:bucket="async" webc:nokeep>
	<h2>Why should you use Eleventy?</h2>
	<p>Fast builds, full control over your output, no client-side JavaScript by default, and no telemetry. <a href="/docs/why/"><strong>Read the full case for Eleventy</strong></a>.</p>

	<h2>News from the Blog</h2>
	<ul @html="getHighlightedBlogPostContent(collections.blog)"></ul>

	<giant-docs-button></giant-docs-button>
	<giant-docs-button-subtext></giant-docs-button-subtext>

	<h2>Built With Eleventy</h2>

	<sites-list>
		<site-card :show-icons="true" size="opengraph" webc:for="(key, site) in shuffle($data.builtwith)" webc:if="!site.disabled && site.featured" :featured="site.featured" :url="site.demo || site.url" :iconUrl="site.iconUrl" :name="site.name" :date="false"></site-card>
	</sites-list>

	<is-land on:visible on:save-data="false">
		<facepile>
			<html-fetch src="/imports/facepile.html"></html-fetch>
		</facepile>
	</is-land>

	<p>A random sample taken from <a href="/authors/"><code><span @text="Object.keys($data.builtwithAuthors).length"></span></code> authors</a>. Check out the <a href="/speedlify/">fastest of their <code><span @text="getsize(objectFilterNot(builtwith, 'disabled'))" webc:nokeep></span></code> web sites</a>.</p>

	<h2>Docs Contributors</h2>

	<is-land on:visible on:save-data="false">
		<facepile>
			<html-fetch src="/imports/docs-facepile.html"></html-fetch>
		</facepile>
	</is-land>

	<p>Thank you to the <code><span @text="docsAuthors.length"></span></code> folks who have contributed to <a href="/docs/">the documentation</a>.</p>

	<h2>Don’t take my word for it <emoji @char="🌈" @alt="Rainbow"></emoji></h2>

	<p>Listen to what these <a href="/docs/testimonials/">happy developers</a> are saying about Eleventy:</p>

	<testimonials-list :@testimonials="testimonials"></testimonials-list>

	<p><a href="/docs/testimonials/">…and many more!</a></p>

	<h2>Alternatives</h2>

	<p>This project aims to directly compete with all other static site generators. We encourage you to try out a few others:</p>

	<lists webc:nokeep>
		<ul class="inlinelist">
			<li><a href="https://jekyllrb.com/">Jekyll (Ruby)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://gohugo.io/">Hugo (Go)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://hexo.io/">Hexo (JavaScript)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://www.gatsbyjs.org/">Gatsby (JavaScript using React)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://nuxtjs.org/">Nuxt (JavaScript using Vue)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://nextjs.org/">Next.js (JavaScript using React)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://www.bridgetownrb.com/">Bridgetown (Ruby)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://astro.build/">Astro (JavaScript)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://remix.run/">Remix (JavaScript using React)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://kit.svelte.dev/">SvelteKit (JavaScript using Svelte)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://jamstack.org/generators/"><em>More at jamstack.org</em></a></li>
		</ul>
	</lists>
</div>

